# Build artifacts. Datasets, fitted models, registries and baselines are
# outputs, not source: they are large, they are reproducible from the training
# commands, and committing one would put a model in the repository that nobody
# reviewed.
artifacts/*
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# ...with one exception: the released champion, and the registry entry that
# says it is the champion. The image has to contain a model or the service
# starts with nothing to serve, and a model fetched at boot from somewhere
# else is a second deployment mechanism to get wrong. So exactly one model
# ships, by name, and swapping it is a reviewable diff — which is what the
# rule above was protecting in the first place. Datasets, metrics, plots,
# audits and every other candidate stay out.
!artifacts/models/
artifacts/models/*
!artifacts/models/lightgbm/
artifacts/models/lightgbm/*
!artifacts/models/lightgbm/lgbm-doc07-1/
!artifacts/registry/

# The knowledge snapshot is the exception and IS committed. It is generated by
# `npm run export:knowledge`, but the service loads it at startup and verifies
# its hashes, so the image has to contain a pinned copy — and a reviewer should
# see a fault-library change arrive in a diff.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
